        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "j. A serious health condition for the purpose of family illness means an illness, injury, impairment, physical or mental condition, as described in D.1.i above, of the employee's child, parent or same- or opposite-sex domestic partner which requires the participation of the employee to provide supervision or care during a period of treatment or incapacity including psychological comfort.",
